chaostictool (2.2.4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Henon handoff: the exported recon.json is now written readable by the invoking operator (owned by SUDO_USER) when ChaosticTool runs under sudo, instead of root:600 — so Henon, running as the normal user, can read it. The ownership handback is restricted to the target results tree (or an operator-owned parent) and never applies to an arbitrary path under a root-only directory.
  * Documentation: version references and download links aligned to the 2.2.4 release.

